The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (tcegrp->grp == iommu_group) {
    ret = -EBUSY;
    goto unlock_exit;
}
```
```c
if (table_group_tmp->ops->create_table != table_group->ops->create_table) {
    ret = -EPERM;
    goto unlock_exit;
}
```
```c
goto unlock_exit;
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the code does not properly handle the memory deallocation for the `tce_iommu_group` pointer (`tcegrp`). When an incompatible group is found, the code jumps to `unlock_exit`, which does not free the allocated memory for `tcegrp`, leading to potential memory leaks or double-free errors.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
goto free_exit;
```
```c
if (ret && tcegrp)
    kfree(tcegrp);
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a new error handling case by redirecting to `free_exit` instead of `unlock_exit` when an error occurs after allocating `tcegrp`. This ensures that if an error is encountered, the allocated memory for `tcegrp` is properly freed, preventing memory leaks or double-free errors.

